3. Independent census of primitive necklaces (Lyndon words, Duval), k <= 24
==============================================================================
Lyndon words of length <= 24: 1465020
necklace count of every cell agrees with the Moebius formula.
integer cycles of 3x+1 (k, s, D, x of the Lyndon rotation):
   (1, 0, 1, 0)  min|n| = 0
   (1, 1, -1, -1)  min|n| = -1
   (2, 1, 1, 2)  min|n| = 1
   (3, 2, -1, -10)  min|n| = -5
   (11, 7, -139, -136)  min|n| = -17
comparison with q13_tiers.json for every c <= 199: 166 cycles, 0 values of c disagree

mirror / cousin: integer cycles with k <= 20 of 3x-1 and 5x+1 from the same Lyndon enumeration
   3x-1: [(1, 0, 1, 0), (1, 1, -1, 1), (2, 1, 1, -1), (3, 2, -1, 5), (11, 7, -139, 17)]
   5x+1: [(1, 0, 1, 0), (2, 1, -1, -1), (5, 2, 7, 1), (7, 3, 3, 13), (7, 3, 3, 17)]
   5x-1: [(1, 0, 1, 0), (2, 1, -1, 1), (5, 2, 7, -1), (7, 3, 3, -17), (7, 3, 3, -13)]
   7x+1: [(1, 0, 1, 0), (3, 1, 1, 1)]
   -> 3x-1: the negated 3x+1 list (same cells, same D).  5x+1: unit cells (1,0), (2,1) only;
      its other cycles (1; 13; 17) are 'accidents' with D = 7, 3, 3.

